e cosponsored it and voted Yea on final passage, which passed 220–208.\n- **Why it fits rung 5:** both are single-subject SAVE Act bills. Their operative text says a state \"may not register an individual to vote … unless … the individual provides documentary proof of United States citizenship.\" That covers both parts of the rung: documentary proof, and at registration. Neither vote is near-unanimous.\n- **Her press release (Feb 2026):** coded as her own words but direction-only. Her quote backs \"proof of citizenship and voter ID\" but doesn't say documentary proof or registration, so it doesn't add to the chair.\n- **Missing source:** the release also says she cosponsored the SAVE America Act. That bill's text and roll call aren't in the sources, so I listed them under `needs_source`.\n- **Quote:** I kept her two press-release sentences as a `lever`, tagged `lever-named` (they name the SAVE America Act), and marked it quotable.\n\nSome connectors in this session need sign-in before they can be used: Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Harvey and WorkOS, via claude.ai connector settings. The GitHub server also failed to connect. This task didn't need any of them.","ttft_ms":20530,"type":"result","duration_ms":45989,"uuid":"d998c9f5-3517-463f-82ee-2a4acc3805b3","ttft_stream_ms":1795,"time_to_request_ms":93,"first_content_frame_ms":1795,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
